The [[Geography/Black and White/index|Black and White]] is peopled by shades: shadows in the shape of men and women, walking its streets, standing in its queues and sitting in its seats. They say nothing. Nothing can be felt in that place, living or dead, and none of them has ever been touched. Looked at straight on they thin to almost nothing, and they are clearest at the edge of vision.

They grow more solid the longer a visitor stays, until they are opaque. Now and then one stands still, seems to face the visitor for a moment, and fades back into the crowd.

Some carry a caught sound inside them. A few in the [[Geography/Black and White/Soundscape Theaters|Soundscape Theaters]] sparkle and chime with faint piano music, with moth wing scales floating inside them. Hold a [[Phenomena/Voice Box|voice box]] to one and the scales pull free, and the shades turn hostile. A hostile shade can throw its own head as a missile and grow a new one. They have no bones; killed, they lose their shape and leave their moth scales floating where they stood.
